<title>USA: IBJ Schroder sets CEO succession plan.</title>
<headline>IBJ Schroder sets CEO succession plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBJ Schroder Bank &amp; Trust Co said it has selected Dennis Buchert to succeed Donald McCree as president and chief executive, effective January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>IBJ Schroder, a unit of Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd, said McCree's decision to retire at the end of this year fulfills a long-held desire to step down at age 60. He will remain a director of the company.</p>
<p>Buchert, who is 49 years old, joined the bank in 1994 as executive vice president and chief banking officer, the second highest ranking executive in the firm.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610</p>
